.TH VIBEOS-SOFTWARE 1 "2026-11-18" "vibeos 0.1.1" "VibeOS"
.SH NAME
vibeos-software \- Software: the VibeOS store's app
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vibeos-software
.br
.B vibeos-software \-\-check\-updates
.SH DESCRIPTION
Software shows the catalog of the VibeOS store (vibeos.top, its API version 1) in four tabs: Featured, Apps, Games and
Mine. Featured, Apps and Games have the categories, the store's sections and lists of apps; search suggests apps and
words as they are typed and keeps the recent searches. An app's page has the install button, the rating, the size and
the age rating, the screenshots, the description, what is new, the permissions the app declares (shown for
information: VibeOS does not ask for or limit them yet), the ratings and reviews, similar apps and the package's
details.
.PP
Installing, updating and uninstalling go through App Installer's D-Bus interface
.RB ( vibeos.Installer1 ,
see
.BR vibeos-installer (1)):
polkit asks for the password, Software never sees it. A job goes on when its page is left, and Mine shows it; closing
the window while one runs hides it until the job ends.
.PP
Mine lists the jobs, the updates (with Update all) and All apps: the ones on this device, and, with a store account,
the ones the account had on other devices or before. Software asks the store for updates when it starts, when the
installed packages change and every hour while it is open, on Wi-Fi only, on any network, or only when asked (its
settings); it does not install them by itself. The number of updates shows on the Mine tab.
.PP
Without the window, the user timer
.B vibeos-software-updates.timer
(enabled for every user by the package) runs
.B vibeos-software \-\-check\-updates
ten minutes after login and every six hours, at a random point of the next half hour; a run missed while the device
was off or asleep happens when it is back. It reads the installed packages, asks the store, and posts one notification
when the store has a version it has not suggested before: "Clock can be updated", or "3 apps can be updated" with
their names. Tapping it opens Software on Mine. A version is suggested once, by the notification or by Mine showing
it; a newer version of the same app is suggested again. The update setting applies: "never" asks nothing, and "wifi"
asks nothing on a metered network. Without a notification server (no graphical session) it asks nothing either.
.B systemctl \-\-user disable \-\-now vibeos\-software\-updates.timer
turns it off for one user.
.PP
A store account (signed up and confirmed with a 6-digit code the store emails) rates and reviews apps, marks reviews
helpful and reports them. The store sets the rules: when it refuses something, its own reason is shown. Signed in, the
store learns this device (a random id, the model, the VibeOS release and the architecture) and the catalog's apps
installed on it. Settings and About are on the account's page, signed in or not.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.cache/vibeos-software/api/
The store's answers with their ETags: a screen is drawn from them at once and asked for again in the background.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/vibeos-software/images/
Icons and screenshots (their addresses never change their bytes).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/vibeos-software/device-id
This device's random id for the store.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/vibeos-software/suggested-updates
The updates already suggested, one package and version per line: the notification does not tell them again.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/vibeos-software/account.json
The signed-in account's name and address (0600), for Mine offline. The account's token is kept in the login keyring
(the Secret Service) under the schema vibeos.Software.Token, with the store's address as its attribute; without a
Secret Service it is kept for the session only.
.PP
The settings are in the GSettings schema
.BR vibeos.Software :
update-mode (wifi, always or never), vibeos-only, color-scheme (system, light or dark) and recent-searches.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B VIBEOS_STORE_URL
The store's address, https://vibeos.top unless set (a local copy of the server, for tests). For the timer's checks,
set it in a drop-in for vibeos-software-updates.service.
.TP
.B VIBEOS_SOFTWARE_TOKEN_FILE
Keeps the account's token in this file (written 0600) instead of the login keyring, for tests.
.TP
.B VIBEOS_SOFTWARE_DPKG_STATUS
Reads the installed packages from this file instead of
.IR /var/lib/dpkg/status .
.TP
.B VIBEOS_SOFTWARE_PAGE
Steps walked once the window shows, separated by semicolons, such as
.B tab:apps;app:org.gnome.Maps;scroll:800
(the list is in the source, apps/software/src/sw-window.c), for pictures and tests.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vibeos-installer (1),
.BR systemd.timer (5)
